{
  "slug": "2027-cola-federal-military-retirees",
  "metaTitle": "FERS COLA 2027 Is 2.6% While CSRS and Military Get 3.6%",
  "metaDescription": "FERS COLA 2027 (cost-of-living adjustment) is 2.6% for eligible annuitants; CSRS and military retired pay get 3.6%. VA disability awaits Congress.",
  "h1": "FERS COLA 2027 (Cost-of-Living Adjustment) for Federal and Military Retirees",
  "cardBlurb": "The 2027 cost-of-living adjustment (COLA) is 2.6% for eligible FERS annuitants and 3.6% for CSRS and military retirees, while VA disability compensation waits on Congress.",
  "introText": "The Federal Employees Retirement System (FERS) cost-of-living adjustment (COLA) for 2027 is 2.6%, while Civil Service Retirement System (CSRS) annuitants and military retirees get the full 3.6%. The 2.6% FERS increase reaches annuitants age 62 or older, plus disability retirees, special-provision retirees and survivor annuitants. The FERS annuity supplement gets no COLA.\n\nThe [Social Security Administration (SSA)](https://www.ssa.gov/news/en/press/releases/2026-10-14.html) announced the 3.6% Social Security COLA on October 14, 2026. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) disability compensation has no automatic COLA and rises only after Congress passes [this year's Veterans' Compensation Cost-of-Living Adjustment Act](https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4487). That bill had not been signed as of October 14, 2026.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "2027 COLA by Retirement System",
      "body": "The 2027 COLA is 3.6% for Social Security, CSRS annuities and military retired pay. Eligible FERS annuities and Career Status Bonus (CSB) retired pay, often called REDUX, get 2.6%. VA disability compensation has no 2027 figure until Congress passes the annual COLA act.\n\nThe Social Security figure comes from the change in the Consumer Price Index for Urban Wage Earners and Clerical Workers (CPI-W) from the third quarter of 2025 through the third quarter of 2026, according to the [SSA fact sheet](https://www.ssa.gov/news/en/cola/factsheets/2027.html). [FEDweek](https://www.fedweek.com/fedweek/january-retirement-colas-set-3-6-percent-for-csrs-2-6-percent-for-fers/) and [Federal News Network](https://federalnewsnetwork.com/retirement/2026/10/2027-cola-is-3-6-for-many-retirees-but-some-feds-will-see-a-smaller-adjustment/) report 3.6% for CSRS annuitants and 2.6% for eligible FERS annuitants.\n\n| Payment | 2027 COLA | Who gets it / condition | Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Social Security | 3.6% | Social Security beneficiaries | Change in CPI-W, third quarter 2025 to third quarter 2026 |\n| CSRS annuity | 3.6% | All CSRS annuitants; first increase prorated at 1/12 per month payable | 5 U.S.C. 8340 |\n| FERS annuity | 2.6% | Age 62 or older, or retired on disability, under special provisions, or receiving a survivor annuity | 5 U.S.C. 8462: price change minus 1 point when above 3% |\n| FERS annuity supplement | No COLA | Not increased | Supplement excluded from the COLA |\n| Military retired pay | 3.6% | Military retirees outside CSB/REDUX | 10 U.S.C. 1401a |\n| Military retired pay, CSB/REDUX | 2.6% | First became members on or after August 1, 1986 and elected the Career Status Bonus | 10 U.S.C. 1401a: price change minus 1 point when above 1% |\n| VA disability compensation | Pending | Needs this year's COLA act; S. 4487 unsigned as of October 14, 2026 | Annual act of Congress |\n\nCSRS annuitants and military retirees outside the CSB/REDUX group get the 3.6% in full. FERS annuitants get 1 percentage point less, and only if they meet the age rule or an exemption. The [2027 Social Security COLA guide](/guides/2027-social-security-cola/) shows what the 3.6% adds to Social Security checks."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why the FERS COLA Is 2.6% in 2027",
      "body": "FERS annuities rise 2.6% because [5 U.S.C. 8462](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/5/8462) subtracts 1 percentage point from any price-index increase above 3%. The statute sets three tiers:\n\n- A change of 2% or less raises the annuity by the full change.\n- A change above 2% and up to 3% raises the annuity by 2%.\n- A change above 3% raises the annuity by the change minus 1 percentage point.\n\nThe 2027 change is 3.6%, which lands in the top tier. The top tier gives 3.6% minus 1 point, or 2.6%.\n\nThe same formula gives different results at other rates, shown here only as an illustration. At a 2.5% change, a FERS annuity would rise 2%, a gap of 0.5 point. At a 1.8% change, a FERS annuity would rise the full 1.8%.\n\nCSRS annuities under [5 U.S.C. 8340](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/5/8340) carry no such subtraction, which is why CSRS retirees get the full 3.6%. The FERS annuity supplement gets no COLA at all, according to Federal News Network. Only the FERS annuity itself rises."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The FERS Age-62 Rule and Its Exemptions",
      "body": "A FERS annuitant who was under age 62 on December 1, 2026 does not get the 2027 COLA unless one of the exemptions in 5 U.S.C. 8462 applies. The statute exempts three groups from the age rule:\n\n- Annuitants who retired on disability\n- Special-provision retirees covered by the statute, such as law enforcement officers, firefighters and air traffic controllers\n- Survivor annuitants, who get the increase\n\nAn annuitant in any of those groups gets the 2.6% effective December 1, 2026. An annuitant outside those groups who was 62 or older on that date also gets the 2.6%.\n\nA regular FERS retiree who was 60 on December 1, 2026 gets no 2027 increase on the annuity. Your own result depends on two facts: your age on December 1 and your retirement type."
    },
    {
      "heading": "CSRS COLA and First-Year Proration",
      "body": "CSRS annuitants get 3.6% for 2027 under 5 U.S.C. 8340, with a smaller first increase for recent retirees. The statute raises each CSRS annuity every December 1 by the percent change in the price index for the base quarter, which ends September 30. The change is rounded to the nearest one-tenth of a percent.\n\nA retiree's first increase is prorated at 1/12 of the percent for each month the annuity was payable before the increase. Proration stops at 12 months, so an annuity payable for a full 12 months gets the whole 3.6%. Only the first increase is prorated under the statute.\n\nTake an annuity first payable 6 months before December 1, 2026. The retiree's first increase is 6/12 of 3.6%, which equals 1.8%. An annuity payable for 3 months gets 3/12 of the increase, or 0.9%."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Military Retirement COLA for 2027",
      "body": "Military retired pay rises 3.6% for 2027, effective December 1, 2026, under [10 U.S.C. 1401a](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/10/1401a). The statute ties the increase to the Consumer Price Index for the base quarter ending September 30, rounded to the nearest one-tenth of a percent. CSRS uses the same base quarter.\n\n[Military Times](https://www.militarytimes.com/pay-benefits/mil-money/2026/10/14/heres-the-2027-cost-of-living-increase-for-retirees-veterans/) gives the example of a military retiree receiving $2,500 in retired pay, who would see about $90 more per month. The math is $2,500 multiplied by 0.036, which equals $90.\n\nRetirees who first became members on or after August 1, 1986 and elected the Career Status Bonus, the REDUX group, get a smaller raise. Their COLA is the price-index percent minus 1 percentage point whenever that percent exceeds 1%. For CSB/REDUX retirees, 3.6% minus 1 point equals 2.6%.\n\nTo estimate retired pay under your own service record, use the [military retirement calculator](/retirement/military-retirement-calculator/). For the tax treatment of disability retired pay, read the guide on [whether military disability retirement pay is taxable](/guides/is-military-disability-retirement-pay-taxable/)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "VA Disability Compensation and the Pending COLA Act",
      "body": "VA disability compensation has no automatic COLA, so its 2027 increase depends on Congress passing the annual Veterans' Compensation Cost-of-Living Adjustment Act. The Senate version this year is S. 4487, introduced on May 11, 2026 and referred to the Senate Committee on Veterans' Affairs. S. 4487 would raise three payments by the same percentage as the Social Security COLA:\n\n- VA disability compensation\n- Dependency and indemnity compensation (DIC)\n- The clothing allowance\n\nThe bill's increase would take effect December 1, 2026. With the Social Security COLA at 3.6%, enactment would mean a 3.6% increase for those payments. Military Times reports that veterans' benefit recipients are slated for the 3.6% COLA.\n\nAs of October 14, 2026, S. 4487 had not been signed into law. VA has published no 2027 rate table, so no 2027 dollar amounts for VA compensation are available. You can follow the bill's progress on its [Congress.gov page](https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4487).\n\nIf you receive both retired pay and VA compensation, the [military retirement vs VA disability](/compare/military-retirement-vs-va-disability/) comparison covers how the two payments differ."
    },
    {
      "heading": "When the 2027 Increase Shows Up",
      "body": "Federal annuity COLAs take effect December 1, 2026 and appear in payments made in January 2027, according to FEDweek and Federal News Network. That timing applies to both the 3.6% CSRS increase and the 2.6% FERS increase.\n\nMilitary retired pay is effective December 1, 2026. VA compensation changes only after this year's COLA act becomes law. If S. 4487 is enacted as introduced, its effective date is December 1, 2026.\n\nSupplemental Security Income (SSI) recipients see the Social Security COLA starting with the December 31, 2026 payment. The [2027 Social Security changes](/guides/social-security-changes-2027/) guide covers the other 2027 Social Security updates."
    },
    {
      "heading": "What to Check on Your Own Payment",
      "body": "Your 2027 increase depends on your retirement system, your retirement type and, under FERS, your age on December 1, 2026. At ModernWallet, we publish free retirement calculators, so you can plug in your new payment without signing up. Work through these steps first:\n\n1. Match your payment to its row in the table above: Social Security, CSRS, FERS, military retired pay, CSB/REDUX or VA compensation.\n2. Under FERS, note whether you were 62 or older on December 1, 2026, or retired on disability or under special provisions.\n3. Under CSRS, if this is your first increase, count the months your annuity was payable before December 1, 2026. Multiply 3.6% by that count, then divide by 12.\n4. Multiply your current monthly payment by 0.036 for a 3.6% raise. Use 0.026 for a 2.6% raise.\n5. For Social Security, read your COLA notice or sign in to [my Social Security](https://www.ssa.gov/myaccount/).\n6. For VA compensation, wait until S. 4487 or this year's COLA act becomes law before counting on a new rate.\n\nOnce you have applied the FERS COLA for 2027 to your monthly annuity, enter the new amount in the [pension calculator](/retirement/pension-calculator/)."
    }
  ],
